{"kind":"request","text":"Security R1, R2, R3 and R12 (6dd06d03 sections 1, 3 and 5): creation and admission.\n\nWork:\n1. R1, gated creation. On a deployed Worker (DEPLOYMENT set), POST /v1/scopes accepts only the install of the pinned register (ARTIFACTS_CONFIG.registerScope) and a creation that the pinned register's judgment produced. Any other install or `found` is refused before any state is written. One explicit deployment setting opens creation, for local and test deployments only, and its name and default go in the head's report. A directory with no creator is refused on a deployed Worker (3.11). Founding policy `open` with a `founders` list is refused at validation (3.12).\n2. R2, no object before proof. A request that names a scope ID with no verified genesis runs no SQLite statement and writes nothing. This covers /v1/scopes/:id, /site/:id, /applications/:id, the hosted MCP registry for a membership ID, and a foreign fact that an act names. Use an index of known scope IDs, or create the tables in the genesis write. State the choice and its cost per request.\n3. R3, turn order. When the signer's authority observation already fails, the act is refused `unauthorized` before any foreign fetch and before the timed drain. The timed drain runs from the alarm, never because an unauthorized act arrived. The per-run `kept` observation map (packages/scope/src/authority.ts:115, :252) gets a bound, and a run above it stops with `limit`.\n4. R12, limits. A per-key and per-address window for creation and for signed reads, like JoinLimits (packages/scope/src/limits.ts). Joins that arrive with no address, from hosted agents in process or through a service binding, count by key.\n\nWitnesses:\n- A fresh keypair's install and `found` on a deployed configuration are refused, and no Durable Object storage is written (1.1, 1.2).\n- For each route in finding 1.2, a request for an unknown scope ID writes no table (1.2, 1.5 registry half).\n- An act by a key with no grant causes no foreign fetch and no timed entry (1.3).\n- A run above the `kept` bound stops with `limit` (1.3).\n- Creation and signed reads refuse the request above the window, per key and per address; a hosted agent's join counts by key (1.6, 3.9).\n- Founding policy `open` with `founders` is refused (3.12).\n- With the opening setting, every existing local and test flow passes. Room creation, join and acts on artroom-scope and dap-grow work after the head (deployable check).\n\nCloses 1.1, 1.2, 1.3, the registry half of 1.5, 1.6, 3.9, 3.11 and 3.12.\n\nCommon conditions (6dd06d03, review of main 603220b9). Checker review of each exact head before it lands. A head can close part of this request; each head names the findings it closes. The hosted Workers (artroom-scope, dap-grow, dap-lending) stay deployable after each head: the head's report lists every new setting and redeploy step, and the planner deploys after review. No deployment by the builder. Place in the security order: 3 of 10 (6dd06d03 assert lists the order). The archive slices keep priority when one of them is ready to work: F1, 9a, slice 9, F2 (land by 4 November) and F3 (deploy by 6 November).","body":{"conditions":"Gated creation, no object before proof, turn reorder, creation and signed-read limits; closes 1.1, 1.2, 1.3, 1.5 registry half, 1.6, 3.9, 3.11, 3.12. Checker review on every head; hosted Workers stay deployable; no builder deployment.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}